      },
      "message": "ci(release): build Windows in parallel and publish from a final job\n\nThe release job (windows-latest) needed linux, macos, snap and flatpak and\nboth built the Windows zip/installer and published the release, so Windows\nstarted only after the slowest job and any failed package meant no Windows\nasset and no release page.\n\nNew graph:\n- windows (windows-latest, no needs): build, sign (secret handling as\n  before), zip + installer, version check from post.exe; uploads\n  portable-zip and installer, exposes the version as a job output.\n- linux (ubuntu-22.04, no needs): uploads linux-packages (unchanged).\n- macos (macos-15, no needs): uploads macos-packages (unchanged).\n- snap, flatpak (ubuntu-22.04, needs linux): upload snap-package and\n  flatpak-package (unchanged).\n- publish (ubuntu-latest, needs all five, if !cancelled() and a tag ref,\n  the only job with contents: write): downloads every artifact that exists\n  into dist/, reads the version from cargo metadata (cross-checked against\n  the windows output when that job ran), runs the RELEASE_NOTES section\n  guard and the release-page template, appends \"Not in this release: ...\"\n  per build job whose result is not success, refuses to publish when no\n  asset exists at all, then publishes with fail_on_unmatched_files: false.\n\nworkflow_dispatch runs still build every platform and publish nothing.\nTop-level permissions drop to contents: read. Triggers are unchanged.\nChecked: YAML parses, the pwsh steps parse; actionlint was not available\nand the workflow itself has not been run.\n\nFixes #125\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
